 $q$-deformed Euler polynomial, is introduced in this paper. This polynomial is defined by the equation:
\begin{equation}
\sum_{n=0}^{\infty} \frac{E_n(q) t^n}{n!} = \frac{2t}{e^t + e^{-t}} \sum_{n=0}^{\infty} \frac{q^n t^n}{n!}.
\end{equation}
This paper explores the properties of these polynomials, including their relationship to the $q$-deformed Bernoulli polynomials, and their connection to the $q$-deformed Euler numbers. Additionally, the paper investigates the properties of the $q$-deformed Euler polynomials, including their symmetry, recurrence relations, and their connection to the $q$-deformed Stirling numbers of the first kind.
